            <div xml:id="d193-a2">

                <pb facs="0339" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg251"/>

                <p>At a meeting of the board of managers of the Lake Carriers’ Association, held at
                    Buffalo, N. Y., on this 18th day of September, 1891, the following resolution
                    was unanimously adopted:</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Resolved</hi>, That the secretary forward to the
                    Department of State, at Washington, the annexed statement or brief relating to
                    tolls on the Welland Canal discriminating against American vessels, ports, and
                    citizens, and respectfully urge the Government of the United States to take
                    prompt and energetic measures in the direction therein indicated to secure to
                    our vessels, ports, and citizens their full rights under the treaty of May 8,
                    1871.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. D. Caldwell</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">President.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>A true copy.</p>
                    <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. H. Keep</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
